WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.560
Hello.

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:10.560
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:17.200
Over the next ten episodes, I will walk you
through the Mood Disorder Guide, step by step.

4
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:22.240
In this first episode, let's look at
what kind of illness a mood disorder is.

5
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:29.250
Mood disorders are commonly known
as depression, or manic depression.

6
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:35.410
Depression means a low mood, with less interest
and motivation, more negative thoughts,

7
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.060
slowed thinking and movement, and
changes in eating and sleeping.

8
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:47.880
Manic depression got its name because an elevated
mood, mania or hypomania, and a sinking mood,

9
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.630
depression, appear in alternation.

10
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:57.560
Because the mood moves between two poles, up
and down, doctors call it bipolar disorder.

11
00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:05.450
But depression and bipolar disorder
are not completely different illnesses.

12
00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:10.710
It is becoming clear that, within
the same group of mood disorders,

13
00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:18.430
they differ only in the balance between a depressive
tendency and a manic-depressive tendency.

14
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:24.673
At one end is typical depression, and
at the other end is bipolar I disorder.

15
00:01:24.693 --> 00:01:30.690
In between are bipolar spectrum
disorder and bipolar II disorder.

16
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:38.150
People with bipolar disorder experience
depression far more often, and for far longer,

17
00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.870
than mania or hypomania.

18
00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:44.230
So when we take another look at someone who was treated

19
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.370
for depression for a long time without getting better,

20
00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.390
it was quite often manic depression all along.

21
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:56.010
Many of these people improve with
specialized treatment for manic depression.

22
00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.260
So even if there are only depressive symptoms,

23
00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:06.610
you should think of bipolar disorder if
any of the following features are present.

24
00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:10.630
A personality prone to mood swings or a hot temper,

25
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:15.750
or moods that change greatly with
the seasons or the menstrual cycle.

26
00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:21.450
Depression that began at a young
age or has come back several times,

27
00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.810
or a history of postpartum depression.

28
00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:30.860
Little effect even with enough antidepressant,
or an effect only at the beginning.

29
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.820
A history of self-harm or a suicide attempt,

30
00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.960
or being sensitive in relationships and easily hurt.

31
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.240
Binge eating, alcohol or gambling problems,

32
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.070
or a personality disorder alongside
the mood symptoms also count.

33
00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:55.330
To understand mood disorders, it
helps to know the word episode.

34
00:02:55.550 --> 00:03:00.290
A period when depressive symptoms
stand out is a depressive episode.

35
00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:06.780
A period when elevated symptoms stand
out is a manic or hypomanic episode.

36
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.900
If your mood doesn't normally swing
much, episodes are clearly separated.

37
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.930
If you have marked mood swings,
the boundaries may be blurred.

38
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.360
A depressive episode is a period
of low mood and lost interest.

39
00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:28.390
You are depressed almost every day, and even
enjoyable things are no longer enjoyable.

40
00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:34.310
Your weight may drop or rise a great deal, and
you may be unable to sleep, or sleep too much.

41
00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:39.040
Your body feels sluggish, and you
are weighed down by powerlessness.

42
00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:44.960
You may be overwhelmed by feeling worthless,
by guilt, and by thoughts of wanting to die.

43
00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.450
Your head feels foggy, and you
cannot concentrate on work.

44
00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:56.060
A manic episode is a period when the mood is
abnormally high and you are full of energy.

45
00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.700
It lasts a week or more.

46
00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.860
You don't feel tired even without sleep, you talk more,

47
00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.260
and your thoughts jump frantically
from one thing to another.

48
00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:13.480
Your self-confidence becomes excessive,
and you may get absorbed in risky behavior,

49
00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:17.960
such as reckless spending or aggressive investing.

50
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.090
Many people cannot remember well what
happened during a severe manic period.

51
00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:30.160
A hypomanic episode is a period when
manic symptoms appear in a mild form.

52
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:35.780
A clearly elevated period, different
from usual, lasts 4 days or more.

53
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:41.060
It does not lead to serious relationship
problems or extreme behavior.

54
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:47.950
You may even be more productive or seem more
attractive, so you may remember it as a good time.

55
00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:52.683
Besides, it is short and causes
little trouble in daily life,

56
00:04:52.703 --> 00:04:58.030
so afterward it is hard to
remember that it was hypomania.

57
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.280
A mixed episode is a period that has the characteristics

58
00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.480
of both a depressive episode and a manic episode.

59
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:11.240
The mood changes over a wide range, which is very hard.

60
00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:17.340
Depression and mania must be managed together,
so treatment needs to be more careful,

61
00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.586
and it needs patience.

62
00:05:20.556 --> 00:05:24.816
A mood disorder is not an illness of the mood alone.

63
00:05:24.836 --> 00:05:30.216
Mood, thinking, motivation and
sensation all change together.

64
00:05:30.436 --> 00:05:35.436
Also, mild symptoms are often present
before the illness fully begins,

65
00:05:35.456 --> 00:05:41.746
so it may be mistaken for personality,
as if you had always been that way.

66
00:05:42.716 --> 00:05:48.576
Today we saw that depression and
bipolar disorder lie on one spectrum,

67
00:05:48.596 --> 00:05:54.636
and that a mood disorder changes mood,
thinking, motivation and sensation together.

68
00:05:54.856 --> 00:05:59.016
Next time, we will look at the
symptoms of mood disorders one by one.

69
00:05:59.036 --> 00:06:00.066
Thank you.
